{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "description": "T21-2e: call-site string lane. count_a's `s` is passed a string literal by one caller and an untypable local-call result by another; the closed string edge among typable callers plus subscript-only use selects the String* lane. T22 replaces the one-character Item materialization (`fn_string_ascii_at`) with fn_string_char_eq_ascii, preserving the same String* lane while avoiding allocation for the literal comparison. first's `s` is also passed an array literal, a concrete non-string caller, so it keeps the boxed parameter and the generic subscript. The .txt golden pins that the untypable caller (make(4)) still reaches the slow body correctly on both tiers.",
  "checks": [
    {
      "in_func": "_count_a_#",
      "expect": [
        "call\tfn_string_char_eq_ascii_p, fn_string_char_eq_ascii",
        "call\tfn_len_s_p, fn_len_s"
      ],
      "forbid": [
        "call\tfn_index_p, fn_index",
        "call\titem_at_p, item_at",
        "call\tfn_string_ascii_at_p, fn_string_ascii_at",
        "call\tfn_len_p, fn_len"
      ]
    },
    {
      "in_func": "_first_#",
      "forbid": [
        "call\tfn_string_ascii_at_p, fn_string_ascii_at"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
